 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Sorry to hear that. Weddings get very busy, so it' worth trying to find out who's running behind and contacting them. No, walk in during the signing of the register. The wedding party and family know exactly when that is. Texting is a good idea, just check it's with you when you get in. Many couples share a rental phone for just that. Try to take a shorter route and leave yourself plenty of time. If you' still stuck, every five minutes waiting is an entire song at double time. You' got this. Weddings run behind sometimes, and it's always the guests who end up being late. The couple will understand.",
